# A fighter knocked out in a battle in an arena built by command comes back in that arena's prep room
# (Moddy-Worlds#60), keeps his place in the battle, and is taken back into the arena after the count. Once the battle
# is over, a respawn is the normal one again (the world spawn, far away), because the arena never changes his spawn.
# The arena is built 300 blocks from the world spawn, so the two can't be confused.
# play-timeout: 600
@intent in an arena built by command a fighter knocked out mid-battle comes back in its prep room and stays in the battle; after the battle a respawn is the world spawn again
@world flat seed=12
@continue-on-fail

@step build the arena far from the world spawn
@wait 3s
difficulty hard
difficulty normal
gamemode survival
effect give @s minecraft:resistance 600 4 true
teleport @s ~300 ~ ~
@wait 2s
moddy arena create pit confirm
@expect chat /Built the arena pit/ within 60s
@wait 2s
summon minecraft:marker ~ ~ ~ {Tags:["prep_mark"]}
moddy arena config pit countdownSeconds 3
@expect chat /countdownSeconds for pit is now 3 seconds/ within 10s

@step knocked out in wave 1, back in the prep room with lives left
moddy arena start pit
@expect title Wave 1 of 5 within 20s
kill @s
@expect chat Knocked out! 2 lives left within 10s
@wait 2s
effect give @s minecraft:resistance 600 4 true
@assert execute at @e[tag=prep_mark,limit=1] if entity @s[distance=..6]
@expect actionbar Back in the arena within 10s
@wait 5t
@assert execute at @e[tag=prep_mark,limit=1] if entity @s[distance=..60]
@assert execute if entity @e[tag=moddyarena_wave]

@step out of lives the battle is lost, and he is in the prep room
kill @s
@expect chat Knocked out! 1 life left within 10s
@wait 2s
kill @s
@expect chat no lives left within 10s
@wait 2s
@assert execute at @e[tag=prep_mark,limit=1] if entity @s[distance=..6]
@expect chat The arena is tidy again within 30s

@step after the battle a respawn is the world spawn again
@wait 2s
kill @s
@wait 3s
@assert execute at @e[tag=prep_mark,limit=1] unless entity @s[distance=..100]
